:: os_lecture_d2
<<img "arjun_distracted_lecture.png" "C-207, OS lecture">>
Prof. Desai writes on the board with the confidence of a man whose subject has never let him down. Process synchronization. Semaphores. Deadlock   the four horsemen: mutual exclusion, hold and wait, no preemption, circular wait.

Your notebook is open. Your pen is in your hand. Nothing is written.

Your body is in a plastic chair in C-207. Your consciousness is at a 1,500-year-old temple twenty minutes away, waiting for a girl named Kavya to explain something insane.

Rohit   actually taking notes today, a sure sign of either the end times or a badly failed assignment   glances sideways. //Bhai teri aankhein laal hain.//<span class="gloss-en">Bro, your eyes are red.</span>

<div class="dialogue">"Arjun. A real-world analogy for the dining philosophers problem?"</div>

You stand. "Five philosophers, one fork between each pair. If they all grab the left fork at once, they wait for the right one forever. Deadlock."

<div class="dialogue">"Good. The solution?"</div>

The answer surprises you as it leaves your mouth: "One philosopher has to be different. Pick the forks up in reverse order. Break the symmetry."

<div class="dialogue">"Excellent. Asymmetry resolves the deadlock."</div>

You sit. Write the first words in your notebook today, in the margin: //Asymmetry.// One element breaks the pattern. One person does something different from everyone else. Meera found a way that doesn't follow the rules every other separated couple follows.

<<run setup.flag("os_lecture_done")>>
<<run setup.flag("vit_day_survived_d2")>>
<<beat>>
Lecture ends at eleven. Nikhil's already texting from two rows up: //canteen. pav bhaji. baat karni hai.//<span class="gloss-en">canteen. pav bhaji. need to talk.</span>

<<hubreturn>>


:: arjun_set_alarm_d2
<<img "arjun_anticipation_night.png" "">>
You open the alarm app. New alarm: 4:00 AM. It asks: //Repeat?// You choose //Once.// This alarm is a one-time event. What happens after it goes off is   you don't know. For six months you've known exactly what tomorrow looks like: Maggi, VIT, pining, code, sleep. Tomorrow the pause ends.

You label it: **TEMPLE**. The old 7:00 alarm, //VIT//, you switch off.

<<run setup.flag("alarm_set_4am")>>
<<if setup.has("arjun_outfit_chosen")>><<run setup.flag("preparation_complete")>>Alarm set, shirt chosen. You're as ready as a person can be for something they can't imagine.<</if>>

<<hubreturn>>


:: arjun_wardrobe_d2
The wardrobe: four t-shirts, two shirts, three jeans, one Diwali-emergency kurta.

The blue checked shirt. Meera touched its collar once, in a Koregaon Park coffee shop, on a "group study session" you both lied about   straightened it and said //Yeh blue tujhpe accha lagta hai. Teri aankhon ko kuch karta hai.//<span class="gloss-en">This blue looks good on you. It does something to your eyes.</span>

You take it out. Put it on the bed. Put it back. This is insane   she won't even see you, it's logistics, not romance. You need to look //awake at 5 AM//, a completely different aesthetic problem.

<div class="choices">
<div class="q">What do you wear tomorrow?</div>
<<link "The blue shirt. She noticed it once.">>
	<<set $arjunOutfit to "blue shirt">>
	<<run setup.flag("arjun_outfit_chosen")>>
	<<goto "arjun_wardrobe_d2_after">>
<</link>>
<<link "Black t-shirt. Practical. Anonymous.">>
	<<set $arjunOutfit to "black t-shirt">>
	<<run setup.flag("arjun_outfit_chosen")>>
	<<goto "arjun_wardrobe_d2_after">>
<</link>>
</div>


:: arjun_wardrobe_d2_after
<<if $arjunOutfit is "blue shirt">>The blue shirt goes over the chair back. You feel the ghost of her fingers on the collar.<<else>>The black t-shirt goes over the chair. Anonymous. The right call. Probably.<</if>>

<<if setup.has("alarm_set_4am")>><<run setup.flag("preparation_complete")>>Alarm set, outfit chosen. Ready.<</if>>

The door opens. Rohit   jersey, gym bag, protein shaker. He clocks the clothes on the chair. His eyebrows perform a synchronized ascent. "Date pe ja raha hai kya?"<span class="gloss-en">Are you going on a date?</span>

"Morning walk."

The silence that follows is Rohit's version of a lie-detector test. "...tu? Morning walk? The guy who thinks getting up before 8 is a war crime." He points at the blue shirt. "Jo bhi hai   woh pehn. Tu usme accha lagta hai."<span class="gloss-en">Whatever it is   wear that one. You look good in it.</span> Then he vanishes into the bathroom.

<<hubreturn>>


:: rohit_choice_d2
Rohit sees the 4 AM alarm. He sees the shirt. He sees you staring at the wall with the face of a man running seventeen processes at once. He sits on his cot. Elbows on knees. The Serious Posture.

<div class="dialogue">"Arjun. Mujhe bata."<span class="gloss-en">Tell me.</span></div>

<div class="choices">
<div class="q">Rohit is your best friend</div>
<<link "Partial truth: someone connected to Meera contacted me. Meeting them tomorrow, early.">>
	<<set $arjunToldRohit to "partial">>
	<<run setup.flag("rohit_told_decision")>>
	<<run setup.stat("rel_rohit", 5, "arjun")>>
	<<run setup.stat("rohit_suspicion", 3, "arjun")>>
	<<goto "rohit_choice_d2_partial">>
<</link>>
<<link "Keep quiet. 'Early library thing. Exam prep.'">>
	<<set $arjunToldRohit to "nothing">>
	<<run setup.flag("rohit_told_decision")>>
	<<run setup.stat("rel_rohit", -2, "arjun")>>
	<<goto "rohit_choice_d2_quiet">>
<</link>>
</div>


:: rohit_choice_d2_partial
"Her roommate. Kavya. She called me. I'm meeting her at 5 AM."

Rohit is quiet for ten seconds   rare, and significant, like a monsoon pause.

<div class="dialogue">"Be careful, bhai." The bro-comedy is gone. This is the boy from Pimpri-Chinchwad whose father runs an auto-parts shop, who has never once failed to show up. "Colonel Kulkarni interrogated actual enemies of the state. If he finds out "</div>

"He won't."

<div class="dialogue">"Famous last words. Written on a tombstone in Comic Sans. Main tere saath chalun?"<span class="gloss-en">Should I come with you?</span></div>

"Nahi. This one I do alone."

He nods slowly. "Okay. But agar subah 8 baje tak tu wapas nahi aaya   main tere Aai ko call karunga. And that woman is scarier than the Colonel and the police combined."<span class="gloss-en">If you're not back by 8 AM   I'll call your mother.</span>

He extends a fist. You bump it.

<<hubreturn>>


:: rohit_choice_d2_quiet
"Nothing, yaar. VIT library opens at 6 for exam prep. Thought I'd actually try studying."

Rohit stares at you. Every micro-expression broadcasts //I know you're lying.// But he's Rohit   he respects boundaries even when they're obviously hiding something.

<div class="dialogue">"Theek hai."<span class="gloss-en">Fine.</span></div>

He returns to his cornflakes. The crunch is louder than necessary. A culinary statement of displeasure.

<<hubreturn>>


:: arjun_night_d2
<<img "arjun_anticipation_night.png" "PG room, 4:00 AM alarm set">>
Rohit's back from leg day at 10:45, smelling of iron, unconscious in eight minutes   a personal record.

You lie in bed. Cannot sleep. The anticipation is physical   it lives in your muscles, the hum of a nervous system running at frequencies you didn't know you had.

Tomorrow you'll be in the same room as Meera. Not through a phone screen. In the same air. Close enough to hear her breathe.

<div class="choices">
<div class="q">The last hour before 4 AM</div>
<<link "Let the wanting build. Don't touch yourself. Carry it into tomorrow.">>
	<<goto "arjun_edging_night_d2">>
<</link>>
<<link "Just try, uselessly, to sleep.">>
	<<run setup.flag("arjun_day2_complete")>>
	<<goto "Arjun2DayEnd">>
<</link>>
</div>


:: Arjun2DayEnd
<<run setup.flag("arjun_day2_complete")>>
<<img "arjun_anticipation_night.png" "">>
Sleep comes in fragments. When it comes, you dream of temples and a girl's voice saying //keep an open mind// and hands that aren't yours holding the face of a girl who is everything.

<span class="scene-break"></span>

**End of Day 2   Arjun.**
<div class="thought arjun">Coding <<= $stats.a_coding>> · Rel Meera <<= $stats.rel_arjun_meera>> · Rel Kavya <<= $stats.rel_arjun_kavya>> · Rel Rohit <<= $stats.rel_arjun_rohit>> · Outfit: <<= $arjunOutfit ? $arjunOutfit : "undecided">> · Mood: <<= $mood.arjun>></div>

The alarm is set for 4:00 AM. The Pulsar keys are on the desk. Tomorrow you leave your body.

